 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Not at all. It helps to plan ahead for clean rooms with disposable utensils and little or no dust, and asking wedding guests to help out if few rooms are involved. Offer a whole package including the wedding venue, rooms, and maybe a cake too. That way, you only have worry about your speech. Nothing. Your allergies. Totally understand. Just give the venue a call and ask about the arrangements, and reassure the couple you'll do it if they do. Definitely. A small box of plain crackers and a small bottle of water is polite, and you' have something if you need it. You don't have to be. Just do what feels right for you. If you end up not going, the couple will find out eventually, and they'd appreciate the invitation all the same.",
